{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Can’t you hear the nightbirds crying
[G]Can’t you [C]hear that lonesome [G]dove
[C]Sayin’ [G]won’t you come back darling
[G]To the [C]only one you [G]love
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Meet me out on the mountain
[D][C]Underneath the lonesome [D]pine
[C]Where we [G]vowed we’d love each other
[G]Darlin’ [C]say won’t you be [G]mine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Where the mountain laurels blooming
And the wildwood blossom grow
There we vowed to love each other
In our childhood long ago
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Then I left my little darling
Lord I’ve rambled for too long
Many times I prayed to see her
Now I’m on my way back home
{end_of_chorus}
